{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787441026605607002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"draughty-callous-tanager","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"7992fe1ac52fc7ee910352efbff6ca1b2ac097595e8b40b5f23fc690482f9cd9","event_uuid":"f8f01340-a2ce-4b89-beb3-49c4f9585a86","position":{"commit_sha":"06aa284ecbb8cc5dae10252d3b4db197a064df19","position":"1787431008723408001-f8f01340-a2ce-4b89-beb3-49c4f9585a86"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4db0f308acf09e44690cadd3ee8eaba599d5d663595ff6904154c05744766324","event_uuid":"9148de0a-c5b8-40f8-9803-e9c6824b68f5","position":{"commit_sha":"9a5abde0508dffea999229e8116b0706b074ed50","position":"1787431064756339001-9148de0a-c5b8-40f8-9803-e9c6824b68f5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"959d58baf81e9cf51cb2ac70bba7d36566f4ec619d92cea147af9db977163c22","event_uuid":"66dad192-0362-4586-bd6b-95651770fca9","position":{"commit_sha":"715d11d8be0da5f10b06ef1c7e1b854109c9c46f","position":"1787440018645315001-66dad192-0362-4586-bd6b-95651770fca9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2bc8e8b03c0bdacda03273bd710407d81e75520569b335ddb9e9ff34b2834c59","event_uuid":"2b6c2e85-66b5-458a-83d9-6c00c05e197f","position":{"commit_sha":"c88f0c2652670abf35fdf9feacc68bac81f09616","position":"1787440986797504001-2b6c2e85-66b5-458a-83d9-6c00c05e197f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3dc2da7be229d3091186515ed6bc6020358999aa36e1c296fe6939d4fcb94b56","event_uuid":"4acd96ae-d2d7-4523-b6d3-ffcc7f614787","position":{"commit_sha":"3fa99a2de633db922495f90985956a498280b3fb","position":"1787441026605607001-4acd96ae-d2d7-4523-b6d3-ffcc7f614787"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Additional live evidence of the drain's steady-state cost, plus a scope boundary.\n\nDuring /rebar-debug of the plan-review sign fence (2026-08-22), `rebar doctor` caught a detached enrich_drain child (pid 96630, spawned by the impl-2ddd-b session) holding the advisory enrich-drain lock 437s at 0.0% CPU before exiting -- i.e. blocked in a no-timeout network call (the enrich LLM) INSIDE the advisory lock, not computing. A successor child (pid 41121) then held it 131s+. So under sustained load the drain is near-continuously lock-held, consistent with this ticket's budget-overrun symptom.\n\nScope note for the dedicated-clone remedy (approved on the related drain ticket): isolating the drain in its own tracker clone is the right fix for the drain's OWN latency / long lock-hold here, but it does NOT fix the plan-review sign-fence bug (a83f-6348-a08c-401d). I measured the sign-fence HEAD churn as 100% foreground ticket writes with 0 drain digest commits across 21 collect() windows -- so the two problems have different churn sources and need separate fixes. Keep them decoupled.","timestamp":1787440018645315001}],"created_at":1787431008723408001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9148de0a-c5b8-40f8-9803-e9c6824b68f5","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3d57-602f-0b75-48ee"},{"link_uuid":"2b6c2e85-66b5-458a-83d9-6c00c05e197f","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"3d57-602f-0b75-48ee"},{"link_uuid":"4acd96ae-d2d7-4523-b6d3-ffcc7f614787","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9c72-c44a-3421-45ad"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nEVERY rebar invocation that writes (and reads that reach _store/push.py) under sustained multi-writer load logs 'WARNING rebar.llm.enrich_drain: enrich drain gate check took N ms (> 20 ms budget)' with N observed 339-3589ms on a 5247-ticket store — a permanent, warned-on-every-command steady state.\n\n## Mechanism (proven during /rebar-debug of 3d57-602f-0b75-48ee — see its RCA comment)\n\nmaybe_drain runs on the store write path (src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:398, src/rebar/_store/push.py:594) and calls queue.pending_enrichment (src/rebar/llm/overlap/queue.py:414). The O(1) gate marker (task 4144-75d3) is cleared by EVERY queue append, so under sustained concurrent writes the fast path never engages and every command pays a full queue scan. The 20ms budget (llm/config.py, overlap_drain_gate_budget_ms) was calibrated for the marker fast path, not for the full-scan fallback at this store size; the warning itself is by-design observability ('budget is an observed target, not a cutoff', enrich_drain.py:379-385).\n\n## Decision needed (why this is not folded into 3d57's fix)\n\nFixing this means changing the enrich-drain gate contract — e.g. a marker that tolerates appends (per-ticket dirty set instead of all-or-nothing clear), a store-size-scaled budget, or throttling the warning. That is a design decision on the gate's freshness/latency trade-off, out of scope for the show-stall regression fix.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A recorded decision on the gate contract: append-tolerant marker, recalibrated budget, or throttled warning (with rationale).\n- [ ] Under a 10+-concurrent-writer load on a 5000+-ticket store, the gate check either meets its (possibly recalibrated) budget or warns at a bounded, non-per-command rate.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","3d57-602f-0b75-48ee"],["relates_to","9c72-c44a-3421-45ad"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6148-5d81-8e80-41e8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"enrich-drain gate check runs 17-180x over its 20ms budget in steady state under sustained write load","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f8f01340-a2ce-4b89-beb3-49c4f9585a86","9148de0a-c5b8-40f8-9803-e9c6824b68f5","66dad192-0362-4586-bd6b-95651770fca9","2b6c2e85-66b5-458a-83d9-6c00c05e197f","4acd96ae-d2d7-4523-b6d3-ffcc7f614787"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787441026605607002,"uuid":"fec17ec1-0ab5-44f4-a026-cddc2abc42c0"}